.TH PYX 1 "2026-10-25" "pyx 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pyx \- compile, check and run a subset of Python 3
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pyx
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.PP
.B pyx
.B \-\-version
.RB [ \-\-verbose ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pyx
is the command\-line driver for PyX, a Python 3 implementation with a
JIT and an ahead\-of\-time (AOT) compiler backend.
It parses and type\-checks Python sources with its own frontend, lowers them
to a native program and runs it with the Cranelift JIT, or links a native
executable.
No CPython installation is required to run a PyX program.
.PP
When no command is given a usage message is printed and the process exits
with status 2.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B new \fIpath\fR [\fB\-\-force\fR]
Create a project directory containing
.BR main.py ,
.B pyproject.toml
and
.BR .gitignore .
Without
.B \-\-force
existing non\-empty files are never overwritten.
.TP
.B init \fR[\fIpath\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR]
Scaffold a project in an existing directory.
.I path
defaults to the current directory.
.TP
.B check \fIfile.py\fR [\fIdiagnostic options\fR]
Parse and type\-check
.I file.py
without running it.
.TP
.B run \fR[\fIdiagnostic options\fR] \fIfile.py\fR [\fIprogram arguments\fR]
Compile
.I file.py
with the JIT and run it.
Everything after
.I file.py
is passed to the program verbatim as
.BR sys.argv [1:]
onwards;
.B sys.argv[0]
is the source path.
Diagnostic options must therefore precede the source file, and
.B \-\-
ends option parsing.
.TP
.B gc \fR[\fB\-\-json\fR] \fIfile.py\fR [\fIdiagnostic options\fR]
Compile and run exactly like
.BR run ,
then print cumulative garbage collector statistics to stdout after the
program output.
With
.B \-\-json
the statistics are one JSON object on stdout and diagnostics are rendered
as JSON; otherwise the statistics are a plain text block.
.TP
.B build \fIfile.py\fR [\fIbuild options\fR] [\fIdiagnostic options\fR]
Compile and link a native executable.
.TP
.B test \fR[\fIpaths\fR...] [\fIdiagnostic options\fR]
Run every
.B test_*.py
and
.B *_test.py
file found under
.IR paths .
A test passes when its program exits with status 0; there are no
pytest\-style assertions.
.TP
.B fmt \fR[\fIpaths\fR...] [\fB\-\-check\fR] [\fIdiagnostic options\fR]
Strip trailing whitespace and terminate each file with exactly one newline.
Indentation, intra\-line spacing and line breaks are preserved.
With
.B \-\-check
the files that would change are reported instead of written.
.TP
.B lint \fR[\fIpaths\fR...] [\fIdiagnostic options\fR]
Type\-check every
.B .py
file under
.IR paths ;
the command fails when any file has diagnostics.
.TP
.B clean \fR[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
Remove the project\-local build cache
.B .pyx/cache
and the temporary AOT directory
.BR target/pyx\-tmp .
The rest of
.B target/
is left alone, and missing paths are not an error.
.TP
.B add \fIspec\fR... [\fIuv options\fR]
.TQ
.B remove \fIspec\fR... [\fIuv options\fR]
.TQ
.B sync \fR[\fIuv options\fR]
.TQ
.B lock \fR[\fIuv options\fR]
Forward all arguments verbatim to
.B uv
in the current directory and return the exit status of
.BR uv .
These commands add no options of their own.
.TP
.B doctor \fR[\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR]
Report the C compiler, the runtime static library and the workspace the CLI
will use.
.TP
.B completions \fIshell\fR
Print a completion script for
.I shell
on stdout.
.I shell
is one of
.BR bash ,
.B zsh
or
.BR fish .
The script is static and self\-contained.
.TP
.B help
.TQ
.B \-\-help
.TQ
.B \-h
Print the command summary.
.TP
.B \-\-version
.TQ
.B \-V
Print
.B pyx
followed by the workspace version.
With
.B \-\-verbose
additional lines report the build target
.RI ( architecture \- operating\ system ),
the backend
.RB ( Cranelift ),
the runtime version
.RB ( runtime: workspace
.I version
.RB ),
and the implemented Python compatibility mode.
.SH OPTIONS
Options are positional: each command accepts only those listed for it.
.SS Global options
Accepted before the command name and, for compiler and project commands, also
before the command's first path.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Print phase timings for
.B run
and
.B build
(frontend, JIT, codegen and link) and the build cache key/hit/miss decisions
on stderr.
With
.B \-\-version
it adds the target, backend, runtime and Python compatibility lines.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress non\-error status output such as scaffold, formatting and removal
messages, and passing test lines.
Errors and diagnostics are always printed.
.PP
.B \-\-verbose
and
.B \-\-quiet
cannot be combined; doing so is a usage error with exit status 2.
.SS Diagnostic options
Accepted by
.BR check ,
.BR run ,
.BR gc ,
.BR build ,
.BR test ,
.BR lint
and
.BR fmt .
.TP
.B \-\-json
Render diagnostics as a JSON array on stderr.
For
.B test
the per\-file results are a JSON array on stdout;
for
.B lint
the aggregated diagnostics are a JSON array on stderr.
.TP
.BI \-\-color= WHEN
Colorize diagnostics.
.I WHEN
is
.BR auto ,
.B always
or
.BR never .
The default is
.BR auto ,
which colors only when stderr is a terminal and
.B NO_COLOR
is unset.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable colors; same as
.BR \-\-color=never .
.SS Build options
.TP
.BI \-o " OUT"
.TQ
.BI \-\-output " OUT"
Output path of the executable
(default: the source file stem in the current directory).
.TP
.BI \-\-runtime\-lib " PATH"
Path to
.BR libpyx_runtime.a .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cache
Do not read or write the build cache under
.BR .pyx/cache .
.SS Project options
.TP
.B \-\-force
Allow
.B new
and
.B init
to overwrite existing non\-empty files.
.SS Path discovery
The
.BR test ,
.B fmt
and
.B lint
commands default to the current directory and search it recursively.
Hidden entries,
.BR target ,
.B __pycache__
and
.B node_modules
are skipped; explicit file arguments are always used as given.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
User or program error: a diagnostic, a failed program, or an I/O failure.
For
.BR add ,
.BR remove ,
.B sync
and
.BR lock
the exit status is the one returned by
.BR uv .
.TP
.B 2
Usage, setup or internal error, including a compiler panic (ICE).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CC
C compiler used by
.B build
to link the executable (default:
.BR cc ).
.TP
.B PYX_RUNTIME_LIB
Path to
.BR libpyx_runtime.a ;
overridden by
.BR \-\-runtime\-lib .
.TP
.B PYX_UV
.B uv
executable used by
.BR add ,
.BR remove ,
.B sync
and
.B lock
(default:
.BR uv ).
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set, colored diagnostics are disabled unless
.B \-\-color=always
is given.
.TP
.B PYX_EXTENSION_PATH, PYTHONPATH, PYX_SITE_PACKAGES
Path lists of directories searched for compiled extension modules
.RI ( name .so,
.IR name .abi3.so ,
.IR name .* .so)
after the importing source file's own directory.
.TP
.B VIRTUAL_ENV, CONDA_PREFIX
Prefixes of virtual environments whose
.I lib/python*/site\-packages
(or
.IR Lib/site\-packages )
directories are searched for compiled extension modules.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B .pyx/cache
Project\-local build cache.
Removed by
.BR "pyx clean" ;
not read or written when
.B \-\-no\-cache
is given.
.TP
.B target/pyx\-tmp
Temporary directory used while linking AOT executables; removed by
.BR "pyx clean" .
.SH COMPATIBILITY
PyX implements a deliberately limited subset of Python 3 and its standard
library; it is neither fully Python\-compatible nor production\-ready.
Unsupported syntax and modules are rejected by the frontend with
.B error[PYXnnnn]
diagnostics.
See the "Language and Stdlib Scope" section of the README and
.I docs/COMPATIBILITY.md
for the supported syntax, bundled modules and the stdlib import matrix.
.SH SEE ALSO
.I docs/DIAGNOSTICS.md
(diagnostic codes, spans, JSON schema and exit codes),
.BR uv (1),
.BR cc (1)
